<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 2324 0 R
  /Alt (The image illustrates two distinct data representations from the EU-Hydro hydrographic database for a river feature. The `River_Net_p` layer is depicted as a blue polygon, representing the wider extent of the river. The `River_Net_l` layer is shown as a yellow line feature, centrally embedded within the `River_Net_p` polygon, likely representing the river's centerline. This visual demonstrates the relationship between polygon and line vector data for river networks, which are used in the Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS) WIC S1 product preparation for categorising river areas.)
